<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Synthetic Lanelet2 fixture: two incoming roads merge into one group of
  adjacent connecting lanelets (the fan-in counterpart of junction_fanout_mini).

  Layout (looking from above, driving direction +x, lanes about 3.5 m wide):
    incoming  X  (id 5101, one lane, straight)          local_x 81700 -> 81720
              Y1/Y2 (ids 5102-5103, two lanes, from the lower left)
    junction  J1/J2/J3 (ids 5104-5106)   local_x 81720 -> 81735, turn_direction=straight
    outgoing  A1/A2/A3 (ids 5107-5109)   local_x 81735 -> 81755
  X continues into J1, Y1 and Y2 into J2 and J3; all three continue into A.
  X and Y share the node where J1 and J2 meet but no boundary way, so they are
  two roads, while J1-J3 are laterally adjacent.

  The connecting road can carry a single road-level <predecessor> (X); the
  lanes coming from Y must not emit <predecessor id> values that only exist
  in Y, because they are read against X.

  Node lat/lon place the layout (local_x -> east, local_y -> north); the
  local_x/local_y tags follow the other mini fixtures and are not read.
-->
